 ## API
 
-- `parse(text)`: milliseconds from a duration made of `h`, `m`, `s` and `ms`
-  parts. Throws `TypeError` on empty input and `SyntaxError` on anything else
-  it cannot read.
-- `format(ms)`: the largest units first, separated by spaces. `0` is `"0s"`.
+- `parse(text)`: milliseconds from a duration made of `d` (24 hours), `h`, `m`,
+  `s` and `ms` parts. Throws `TypeError` on empty input and `SyntaxError` on
+  anything else it cannot read.
+- `format(ms, options?)`: the largest units first, separated by spaces. `0` is
+  `"0s"`. Hours are the largest unit by default (`25h`); pass `{ days: true }`
+  to show whole days: `format(93600000, { days: true })` is `"1d 2h"`.
 
 ## Versioning
 
